      "knowledge_point_id": "905d1f6a-72aa-5984-8c7d-920497fd58e4",
      "knowledge_point": "Differentiating Inverse Reciprocal Trigonometric Functions Using the Product Rule",
      "problem": "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ for $f(x)=arccscx\\cdot arcsecx$",
      "worked_solution": "The formulae for the derivatives of $arccsc$ and $arcsec$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arccscx) & =-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arcsecx) & =\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule and the formulae above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =arcsecx\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arccscx)+arccscx\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arcsecx) \\\\  & =arcsecx\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}})+arccscx\\cdot (\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{arcsecx}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}+\\frac{arccscx}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{arccscx-arcsecx}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
