      "problem": "Calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $y=\\frac{arccscx}{{e}^{3x}-1}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Here, we let $u(x)=arccscx$ and $v(x)={e}^{3x}-1$, and apply the quotient rule.\n\nWe use the formulae\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}(x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{and}\\,{v}^{′}(x)=3{e}^{3x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\cdot ({e}^{3x}-1)-arccscx\\cdot 3{e}^{3x}}{({e}^{3x}-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{({e}^{3x}-1)|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}-\\frac{3{e}^{3x}arccscx}{({e}^{3x}-1)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
