      "math_academy_id": "q-8027",
      "knowledge_point_id": "e73b8bcf-79c2-5326-b396-d7d3e06badaa",
      "knowledge_point": "Identifying the Standard Matrix of a Linear Transformation",
      "problem": "Find the standard matrix that  represents  the  linear  transformation $T$, where\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}2x-y \\\\ x-y\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "We require a $2\\times 2$ matrix $T$ such that\n    \n\n$$\nT\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot x+(-1)\\cdot y \\\\ 1\\cdot x+(-1)\\cdot y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2x-y \\\\ x-y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n    Therefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $T$ is\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
